                <pb facs="0284" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg188"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-08-28"><hi rendition="#italic">August 28,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee directs Mr. Conger to consult General Chaffee with a view to
                    ascertaining, if possible, the fate of Americans at Paoting, reports regarding
                    which are conflicting; and, if any are alive, to report, dating his telegram, if
                    relief can be given.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
